ood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify that batching/deferred-push/partial-recovery/concurrency prose must be ADDED to the import parser (name the vehicle — description vs. epilog) since build_import currently carries none, and note that docs/import-export.md is a separate authority.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1533,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/io.py:45-55 — build_import has only description='Import tickets from export NDJSON (clean rebar->rebar migration).' and --dry-run/file","src/rebar/_cli/help/import.txt (generated) contains no batching/duplicate/deferred-push prose","The stale 'duplicate creation and future batching' text the Context references is in docs/import-export.md:79-83, not the parser help","epilog is the established vehicle for parser prose (writes.py:129, lifecycle.py:87, advanced/llm.py:150) but only for terse one-liners"],"finding":"The plan assumes the canonical import parser help already carries batching/duplicate/deferred-push prose to 'update', but build_import currently exposes only a one-line description plus --dry-run/file; the stale prose actually lives in docs/import-export.md. Satisfying the ACs ('Canonical import help describes current batching / deferred-push behavior', partial-results, no-atomicity, concurrency limits) therefore requires ADDING multiple paragraphs of new prose to the parser via description or epilog — a mechanism decision the plan never names.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4c3b44135fd6f595","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 'Update canonical import parser help before generated artifacts'; AC 'Canonical import help describes current batching behavior' / 'deferred-push behavior'","norm_id":"n310b6270dd4bbca1","priority":0.4467,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer reads 'update' as edit-existing, discovers there is nothing to update, and either under-delivers (leaves ACs unmet) or improvises the prose vehicle"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State explicitly that the canonical prose will be authored into build_import's epilog (mirroring writes.py/lifecycle.py), enumerate the topics it must cover, and clarify that docs/import-export.md is corrected independently.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the Context to state where the stale text actually lives: the 'future batching / no batch-commit primitive' claim is in docs/import-export.md (L79-83), the canonical parser help (io.py) and packaged import.txt are currently terse with no batching/duplicate wording, and no 'duplicate creation' claim exists in the import help.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.42,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Canonical parser help src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/io.py build_import (L45-55) has only description='Import tickets from export NDJSON (clean rebar->rebar migration).' — no duplicate-creation or batching text.","Packaged src/rebar/_cli/help/import.txt (whole file) is a 9-line usage block with no duplicate/batching wording.","search_files for 'duplicate' under src/rebar/_cli/help returns only link.txt/overview.txt (relation vocabulary), never import help.","The 'future batching' claim actually lives in docs/import-export.md L79-83: 'KNOWN LIMITATION: there is currently no batch-commit primitive... A batch-commit primitive is deferred to a follow-up task.' — a DOCS surface, not the help.","docs/import-export.md L69 states the opposite of duplicate creation: 'Re-runs and resume-after-crash never duplicate.'"],"finding":"The Context premise 'Import help still describes duplicate creation and future batching' is not borne out by the code: the canonical import parser help and packaged help contain neither, and the stale 'future batching' wording lives only in docs, not the help.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f20cbeba7761e480f","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context section, sentence 1 ('Import help still describes duplicate creation and future batching.')","norm_id":"ndbb0e88941dcd3ea","priority":0.33,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An author reads the Context to locate stale text in the parser/packaged help and finds none, wasting effort or mis-editing the wrong surface.","A reviewer treats the Context as the work inventory and under-scopes the docs correction that actually holds the stale batching claim."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Reword Context to: 'The canonical import parser help is terse and silent on batching; docs/import-export.md still carries a stale KNOWN LIMITATION claiming no batch-commit primitive exists and that batching is deferred to a follow-up.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_ca